<title>LEBANON: Lebanese parliament approves 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Lebanese parliament approves 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lebanese parliament approved a 6,433 billion Lebanese pounds ($4.15 billion) state budget for 1997 on Monday with a 36 percent deficit of income against expenditure.</p>
<p>The 128-member parliament voted to approve the budget draft despite a stormy five-day debate in which deputies accused the government of sinking the country in debt and criticised it for repeated budget overruns.</p>
</text>
